Description: Keep the window opened for a launch as it was opened and restore the saved windows into new ones.
 When Firefox starts and restores the previous session, the session store restores the first window of the saved
 session into the window opened for the launch. A URL from the command line, as when a link is opened from another
 application while Firefox is not running, becomes a tab of that window, on whichever workspace it returns to,
 also when browser.link.open_newwindow.override.external (or browser.link.open_newwindow, which it falls back to)
 opens external links in a new window, as they do while Firefox runs. A launch without a URL opens no new window
 either, unlike a launch while Firefox runs.
 .
 The window opened for the launch now keeps its page, the URL or the start page, every saved window is
 restored into a new window, and the window opened for the launch is the one focused afterwards. With a URL this
 follows where external links open. Without one it holds for every start by the user, also a recovery after a
 crash, but not for a restart by Firefox itself (browser.sessionstore.resume_session_once), such as after an
 update, which reopens the windows as they were.
 .
 On Wayland every window opened during startup session restore waits hidden until it is restored, and a window
 which is not restored is shown when session restore finishes (wayland-session-restore-show-waiting-windows.patch).
 The window opened for the launch is thus shown after the restored ones, so the compositor places it on the current
 workspace and focuses it after any restored window there. wayland-launch-activation-token.patch passes it the
 activation token of the launch.
 .
 Related to Mozilla bug 1565050: with external links opening in a tab, the URL opens in the first window of the
 saved session rather than in the last used one.
